\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_016HnJdNetQ2qzVN4MLF3Kcd\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"commit 15a774515f5aae7087031fe02c9b95297bb77ba3\\nAuthor: attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\\nDate:   Sun Sep 27 08:48:47 2026 -0600\\n\\n    attavo: an empty build is not a pass (item 229)\\n    \\n    The gate now reads the commit, never the executor's directory: criteria,\\n    selected tests, and the tenant's checks run in a detached worktree of\\n    HEAD (gate_checkout), so a path written and never committed cannot pass\\n    on the executor's behalf. An iteration that ends with HEAD unchanged\\n    since start_sha is fed back; the last such iteration halts the build\\n    with the new stop class `empty` instead of passing or plain-failing.\\n    Verify refuses a passing build record whose sha equals its start_sha,\\n    and the doctor's seventh proof holds that no attested item's build is\\n    empty, windowed by [doctor].built_since so item 227 (the specimen) is\\n    named before the window rather than failing the tenant forever.\\n    \\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n .github/workflows/ci.yml          |   1 +\\n adapters/fixture/run              |  10 +++-\\n attavo.toml                       |   5 +-\\n attavo/build.py                   | 114 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------\\n attavo/cli.py                     |  32 +++++++++--\\n attavo/doctor.py                  |  72 +++++++++++++++++++++++-\\n attavo/stops.py                   |   2 +-\\n attavo/verify.py                  |   4 ++\\n schema/manifest.schema.json       |   5 ++\\n schema/records/build.schema.json  |   4 +-\\n schema/records/verify.schema.json |   4 +-\\n tests/test_build.py               |  47 ++++++++++++++++\\n tests/test_cli_help.py            |  10 ++++\\n tests/test_doctor.py              |  66 ++++++++++++++++++++++\\n tests/test_own_records_guard.py   |   2 +-\\n tests/test_self_tenancy.py  