st_build.py\n666:diff --git a/attest/specs/229/criteria/an-executor-that-commits-nothing-does-not-pass.sh b/attest/specs/229/criteria/an-executor-that-commits-nothing-does-not-pass.sh\n671:@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@\n720:diff --git a/attest/specs/229/spec.md b/attest/specs/229/spec.md\n725:@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@\n734:+The gate reads the commit. Each iteration's criteria, selected tests and tenant checks run in a detached worktree of `HEAD` (`gate_checkout`: `git worktree add --detach`, removed when the iteration's gate is done), never in the executor's directory. A file written and not committed cannot pass a criterion, a test or a check on the executor's behalf; a tenant checks command that writes beside itself writes into the worktree and is gone with it. The pre-executor probe (`[checks].probe`) still runs against the approved tree in place, as it did.\n736:+An empty iteration is told so. When an iteration ends with `HEAD` equal to `start_sha`, the gate runs (on the approved tree, where the criteria already fail), the log and the feedback both carry \"you committed nothing: no commit since <start>; N path(s) modified or untracked in the working tree, which the gate does not read\" and \"commit your work; the gate reads the commit, not the tree\", and the loop continues. An executor that answers `done` before committing on its first iteration and commits on its second passes as before (`test_an_empty_iteration_is_fed_back_and_a_later_commit_passes`).\n738:+An empty build is halted. When the last iteration ends with `HEAD` equal to `start_sha`, the record is `halted` with a new stop class `empty`, provenance `executor`, detail \"the executor committed nothing; ...\" with the count of paths left in the tree. The class is the executor's, so counsel reads it and a steer retries it under R3; no new family. `STOP_CLASSES` and the build and verify schemas carry `empty` (build/9, verify/8). The status can never be `pass` with `sha` equal to `start_sha`.\n746:+The stub under `stub/` is the change: `gate_checkout` and the empty-iteration handling in `attavo/build.py`, the class in `attavo/stops.py` and the two schemas, verify's refusal, proof seven and the manifest key, the fixture adapter's `ATTAVO_FIXTURE_NO_COMMIT`, the self-tenant's window and deselect, and seven tests red on the tree (v0.29.0). `tests/test_cli_help.py::test_help_names_the_seventh_proof_and_the_empty_stop` is red on the stub by design; the help text is the build's. Four existing tests move with the gate: two in `tests/test_testtool.py` whose checks counter lived in the tree the gate no longer reads, `test_self_tenancy.py`'s assertion that the manifest has no `[doctor]` table, `test_own_records_guard.py`'s deselect count, and `test_stub_ratio.py`'s pinned `verify/7`. `python3 -m mypy` exits 0 on the stub.\n779:diff --git a/attest/specs/229/stub/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/attest/specs/229/stub/.github/workflows/ci.yml\n784:@@ -0,0 +1,186 @@\n971:diff --git a/attest/specs/229/stub/adapters/fixture/run b/attest/specs/229/stub/adapters/fixture/run\n976:@@ -0,0 +1,141 @@\n1083:+  # a commit not authored by the executor identity build exports (issue\n1091:+    commit -q -m \"fixture: a commit not authored by the executor\"\n1118:diff --git a/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo.toml b/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo.toml\n1123:@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@\n1192:diff --git a/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/build.py b/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/build.py\n1197:@@ -0,0 +1,694 @@\n1406:+    \"\"\"(retry_of, steer, feedback): what a retried build's first iteration\n1608:+                \"iterations\": 1,\n1645:+    iterations_used = 0\n1650:+        # R3: a retried attempt's first iteration starts with the prior\n1658:+        for iteration in range(1, BUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET + 1):\n1659:+            iterations_used = iteration\n1660:+            append_event(events_path, \"iteration\", f\"iteration {iteration} of {BUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET}\")\n1670:+            env[\"ATTAVO_ITERATION\"] = str(iteration)\n1717:+            foreign = next((c for c in commits_since(root, start_sha)\n1720:+            if foreign:\n1722:+                refusal = f\"commit {foreign['sha']} not authored by the executor\"\n1727:+            # an empty iteration fails its gate on the approved tree and is\n1728:+            # told why; an empty last iteration is halted, class empty\n1756:+            # behalf (item 227). Removed before the iteration ends.\n1784:+            # per iteration, before this temporary directory goes away --\n1801:+            transcripts[-1] += (f\"\\n--- attavo gates, iteration {iteration} ---\\n\"\n1814:+            if iteration == BUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET:\n1854:+        \"iterations\": iterations_used,\n1892:diff --git a/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/doctor.py b/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/doctor.py\n1897:@@ -0,0 +1,920 @@\n2507:+                        and \"--- attavo gates, iteration\" not in (log or \"\")):\n2818:diff --git a/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/stops.py b/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/stops.py\n2823:@@ -0,0 +1,379 @@\n2974:+        payload once an iteration ends. This is non-question's and\n2999:+        itself, not the \"commit ... not authored by the executor\" shape\n3203:diff --git a/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/verify.py b/attest/specs/229/stub/attavo/verify.py\n3208:@@ -0,0 +1,461 @@\n3670:diff --git a/attest/specs/229/stub/schema/manifest.schema.json b/attest/specs/229/stub/schema/manifest.schema.json\n3675:@@ -0,0 +1,258 @@\n3751:+      \"description\": \"The tenant's own definition of done: a whole-tree check, as the tenant runs it locally. attavo build runs it each iteration, after the claims boundary, the criteria, and the selected tests -- pass requires its exit to be 0, and a non-zero exit reaches the executor as feedback. Optional; a tenant that declares none is not refused (unlike [tests], which build requires).\",\n3757:+          \"description\": \"The tenant's whole-tree check at the gate, run from the tenant root once per iteration on the com